<!--
	Navezgane Hospital Challenge - Sandbox Option Presets
	Author: Frilioth
	Version: 1.0.0

	Puts the Hospital Challenge difficulty tiers in their OWN group in the Sandbox
	Options preset dropdown, alongside Difficulty / Official / User, rather than
	landing in the generic "Modded" group with every other mod's presets.

	WHY THIS NEEDS THE DLL (confirmed by reading the 3.2 assembly, not assumed):
	  Config/sandbox_overrides.xml IS mod-patchable and DOES accept <preset>
	  elements, but SandboxOverridesFromXml always calls LoadPresetFromXml with
	  the group override "Modded". LoadPresetFromXml only reads a preset's own
	  "category" attribute when that override is null or empty, so a category set
	  there is silently ignored. Hospital therefore loads this file itself and
	  passes its own group name.

	GROUP NAME AND LOCALISATION
	  XUiC_SandboxPresetSelector.updatePresetGroups builds each group's display
	  name with Localization.Get(<group name>) - the group name IS the key, and
	  there is no "sandboxPresetGroup" prefix in 3.2. So the group name below has
	  a matching row in this mod's Localization.csv. Without that row the dropdown
	  would show the raw key "HospitalChallenge" instead of "Hospital Challenge".

	HOW TO FILL IN A PRESET
	  1. In game: New Game -> Sandbox Options, set everything the way you want it.
	  2. Use the copy button next to the sandbox code box to copy the code.
	  3. Paste it into code="" below, replacing FILLMEIN.
	  4. Save and restart the game. No recompile needed.

	  A preset whose code is still FILLMEIN is SKIPPED at load, so a half-finished
	  entry never shows up broken in the menu. Fill them in one at a time.

	CURRENT CODES ARE PLACEHOLDER BALANCE, NOT HOSPITAL BALANCE.
	  The six codes below were carried over from another mod's difficulty ladder to
	  give a working starting point rather than six empty tiers. They are settings
	  values only - no code, XML or assets were shared - but they were tuned for a
	  different challenge and should be regenerated for this one.

	  When regenerating, check these in particular, because Hospital's own systems
	  read them:
	    LootRespawnDays  - if a preset sets this to 0, the loot restock timer AND
	                       the "Restocks on Day X" text both switch off entirely.
	                       Both patches check it is > 0 before doing anything.
	                       The design calls for a 5 day respawn.
	    XPMultiplier     - drives how fast Forge Ahead unlocks, which gates the
	                       workbench, chemistry station and dew collector.
	    DeathPenalty     - Hospital enforces permadeath itself; do not rely on the
	                       vanilla option, which is not fully implemented.

	ATTRIBUTES
	  name              required. Internal id, no spaces.
	  code              required. The sandbox code copied from the options screen.
	  description       required (or description_key for a Localization.csv key).
	  localized_name    optional. What players see. Falls back to name.
	  icon              optional. Two forms work:
	                      Data/Sandbox/icons/user_custom          (a vanilla path)
	                      @modfolder(FrilHospitalChallenge):Resources/yourfile.png
	                    Drawn at 180x180 keeping aspect ratio, so square is safest.
	                    Unity sniffs the format rather than trusting the extension,
	                    so a JPEG named .png loads fine and is far smaller.
	  difficulty_rating optional. Shows a skull and "xN" next to the preset.
	                    Keep ascending or the ladder reads oddly.
	  default           optional. "true" marks the default selection for a new game.

	THE LADDER
	  These are difficulty tiers, not per-world settings. The biome is chosen
	  separately from the world list, so one ladder covers all five maps.
-->

<!--
	     PRESET ICONS
	     icon="@modfolder(FrilHospitalChallenge):Resources/<file>" - a plain image
	     file, no asset bundle and no code hook needed. The menu draws the icon with
	     an XUi <texture>, and XUiV_Texture.loadTexture runs the string through
	     ModManager.TryPatchModPathString and loads it as file://, which is why the
	     modfolder form resolves.
	     THE EXTENSION IS IGNORED AND THE FORMAT IS SNIFFED: Unity reads the magic
	     bytes, so a JPEG named .png works and is far smaller. Do not waste time
	     converting. Drawn at 180x180 keeping aspect ratio, so keep them SQUARE.
-->

<!--
	     LOCALISED PRESET NAMES AND DESCRIPTIONS
	     localized_name is NOT literal text - SandboxOptionPreset.DisplayName does
	     Localization.Get(LocalizedName), so whatever is put here is looked up as a
	     KEY. A plain name like "Walk-In" resolves to nothing and the key is echoed
	     back, which LOOKS like working English and is why this went unnoticed.
	     description is literal, but description_key goes through Localization.Get
	     the same way (see DisplayDescription in the assembly).
	     Both now point at keys in Config/Localization.csv, translated into all nine
	     languages. Do not put display text back in either attribute.
-->

